A step is plain SQL, run as written: SQLite will not drop a column a view
still reads, and says which view. The step drops the view first (deploy 2);
schema.sql makes it again, as it is now, after the steps.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW dishes AS SELECT id, name, note FROM dish;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'hot');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW dishes AS SELECT id, name FROM dish;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN note;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE VIEW dishes AS SELECT id, name FROM dish;

== ledger
DROP VIEW dishes;
ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN note;

== plan
-- after 1
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN note;
-- after 2
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's steps 1 to 2
  step 1
    DROP VIEW dishes;
  step 2
    ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN note;
roux: migrating test.db, 1 step
  view `dishes`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE VIEW dishes AS SELECT id, name FROM dish

